{"chunk_id": "4a6210c96844", "text": "This section advances Duryodhana\u2019s plot against the Pandavas. Delighted that Dhritarashtra has sent them to Varanavata, Duryodhana secretly instructs his agent Purochana to build a magnificent palace made of highly flammable materials\u2014lac, resin, oil, hemp, and fat\u2014while disguising it as a luxurious residence. Once the unsuspecting Pandavas settle there with Kunti, Purochana is to burn the house and make their deaths appear accidental. Meanwhile, the Pandavas depart respectfully from the Kuru elders and the citizens, who openly condemn Dhritarashtra\u2019s injustice and express loyalty to Yudhishthira. Despite their grief, Yudhishthira urges the people to obey the king and return home, showing his commitment to duty and restraint even while walking into a deadly trap. The passage contrasts political treachery with moral integrity.\nDuryodhana secretly orders Purochana to build a flammable palace at Varanavata to burn the Pandavas, who depart amid sorrowful farewells from citizens.\nThemes: treachery and conspiracy, political intrigue, loyalty of citizens, duty and obedience, impending assassination", "vector": [0.008993417024612427, -0.009892072528600693, -0.009164915420114994, -0.0061088004149496555, -0.015091927722096443, 0.027535907924175262, -0.027165468782186508, -0.012910458259284496, -0.009295254945755005, -0.010715268552303314, 0.03482119366526604, 0.01938626728951931, 0.011936342343688011, 0.027384988963603973, -0.007340164855122566, 0.011065126396715641, 0.04461722448468208, -0.014913568273186684, 0.033531516790390015, -0.026218794286251068, -0.016820639371871948, 0.0037901317700743675, -0.005247874651104212, 0.027851466089487076, -0.01710875704884529, 0.019468586891889572, 0.012793838046491146, -0.0176163949072361, 0.0061945500783622265, 0.0015143377240747213, -0.005560003221035004, -0.012821278534829617, 0.01835727132856846, -0.015174247324466705, -0.025820916518568993, 0.00608822051435709, -0.00847205